## Run it

```sh
cp .env.example .env
{%- if include_postgres %}
cp .env.database-owner.example .env.database-owner
{%- endif %}
docker compose up -d --build --wait
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

Fill in every key the example env files leave empty. None of them is committed. For day-to-day work without an image
rebuild, see Local development in `BACKEND-API.md`.

## Checks

```sh
uvx prek run --stage pre-push --all-files
```

CI runs the same command, on `ubuntu-latest` unless the repository variable `CI_RUNNER` names other runner labels as
JSON. The e2e flows in `e2e/` run by hand when a change needs one.

## Deploy

On the host, with the env files outside the checkout and mode 600:

```sh
export {{ environment_prefix }}_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=<deploy .env>
{%- if include_postgres %}
export {{ environment_prefix }}_DATABASE_OWNER_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=<database owner env file>
export {{ environment_prefix }}_POSTGRES_BACKUP_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=<backup env file>
{%- endif %}
deploy/deploy.sh
```
{%- if include_postgres %}

Once per host, install the backup schedule's systemd unit (Backup schedule in `BACKEND-API.md`). Until it runs,
`deploy/deploy.sh` deploys, warns and exits 1.
{%- endif %}

## Update from the template

```sh
uvx copier update --trust
```

The tree must be clean. It never overwrites this file or `AGENTS.md`. Each
[release](https://github.com/7331/python-backend-template/releases) lists the steps an update needs by hand.
